+## Explicit findings
+
+- **Coherence — PASS.** All 1,000 tuples keep the selected species, structure or behavior, habitat/life-stage scope, biological mechanism, and evidence method materially connected. No tuple relies on an independently substituted generic axis.
+- **Factual basis — PASS.** Every tuple is grounded in documented anatomy, physiology, behavior, life history, ecology, or a named conservation pressure. Conditional or variable effects are framed as observations, risks, recorded associations, or possible ecological effects rather than universal certainty.
+- **Evidence posture — PASS.** Every tuple names a relevant observation, experiment, anatomy/physiology study, tracking method, survey, or food-web analysis. The pack continues to require episode-level research; no lens is presented as a citation or proof by itself.
+- **Exclusions — PASS.** No tuple assigns human thought, motive, dialogue, or morality to an animal. Defensive and predatory mechanisms are described biologically without unsupported danger claims.
+- **Compatibility — PASS.** The predecessor IDs, two compatible Formula IDs, compatibility rules, prompt context, tags, entitlement family/SKU, lifecycle, publisher, minimum-app placeholder, and empty dependency closure are preserved. The corpus remains a profile-based animal pack for `Natural World, Explained` and `Counted Explainer`; no Formula, Kit, schema, adapter, or planner change is required.
+- **Originality — PASS.** The tuples are newly authored factual summaries. No creator identity, branded wording, title list, reference composition, copyrighted passage, asset, or generated-media output was copied. Shared zoological terms name facts and methods, not borrowed expression.
+- **Safety — PASS.** Venom, predation, disease, poaching, bycatch, and human-wildlife conflict are described at explanatory resolution without operational harm instructions, sensationalized threat, or advice to handle wildlife.
+- **Copy — PASS.** Every episode object is concrete and filmable; every mechanism states causal biology; scopes specify habitat, season, life stage, or interaction; evidence lenses identify a usable research approach. No title-only variants or generic filler carry structural capacity.
+- **Duplicate scan — PASS.** Mechanical scan result: 50 unique subjects; 50 profiles; 1,000 complete tuples; 1,000 unique episode objects; 1,000 unique mechanisms; 1,000 unique `episode_object|mechanism` pairs; 1,000 unique complete subject-bound tuples; 20 unique episode objects and 20 unique mechanisms inside every profile.
+- **Placeholder scan — PASS.** Case-insensitive scan for `TBD`, `TODO`, `placeholder`, `lorem ipsum`, `generic animal`, `various animals`, numbered animal/mechanism filler, and numbered tuple filler returned no matches.
+
+## Final verdict
+
+**PASS for Task 2 source qualification.** The exact successor document bound above supplies 50 concrete animal species × 20 reviewed atomic tuples and preserves the predecessor's identity, compatibility, exclusions, and evidence posture. Publication, stocking, signing, pricing, and Kit mutation remain outside this review.
